SUMMARY:Deadline: International Vouchers
DESCRIPTION:Travel voucher for Dutch-based professionals in design\, archit
 ecture and/or digital culture who have been invited by a foreign party to 
 give a presentation\, lecture or workshop. To apply you must have submitte
 d an application to the Fund in the past five years that was positively as
 sessed (previous International Vouchers do not count).\n\nOrganisation: St
 imuleringsfonds Creatieve Industrie (Creative Industries Fund NL)\nLocatio
 n: Netherlands (for international travel)\nAward: Up to €1\,500 within E
 urope (zone 1) / up to €2\,500 outside Europe (zone 2)\nDuration: Per tr
 ip\n\nMore: https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouch
 ers?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/international-vouchers?utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands (for international travel)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:stimuleringsfonds-suriname-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T230337Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261021
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261022
SUMMARY:Deadline: Stimuleringsfonds: Open Call Residency Suriname 2027 (Par
 amaribo\, Moengo\, Frederiksdorp)
DESCRIPTION:The Creative Industries Fund NL (Stimuleringsfonds) is recruiti
 ng one Netherlands-based designer\, architect or interdisciplinary maker f
 or a three-month residency in 2027 across three locations in Suriname: Par
 amaribo\, Moengo and Frederiksdorp\, each with its own cultural\, historic
 al and social context.\n\nOrganisation: Stimuleringsfonds Creatieve Indust
 rie (Creative Industries Fund NL) with local partner organisations in Suri
 name\nLocation: Residency takes place at three locations in Suriname: Para
 maribo\, Moengo and Frederiksdorp. Applicants must be established in the N
 etherlands\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maa
 rten (Kingdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a business register wi
 thin the Kingdom of the Netherlands.\nAward: EUR 8\,500 subsidy for a thre
 e-month residency\, paid by the Creative Industries Fund NL. One residency
  position is awarded. No application fee.\nDuration: Three months in 2027\
 , moving between Paramaribo\, Moengo and Frederiksdorp\n\nMore: https://ww
 w.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-suriname?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.stimuleringsfonds.nl/en/grants/open-call-residency-suriname
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Residency takes place at three locations in Suriname: Paramaribo\,
  Moengo and Frederiksdorp. Applicants must be established in the Netherlan
 ds\, Aruba\, Bonaire\, Curacao\, Saba\, Sint Eustatius or Sint Maarten (Ki
 ngdom of the Netherlands) and registered in a business register within the
  Kingdom of the Netherlands.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jan-van-eyck-residency-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T230337Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261201T222900Z
DTEND:20261201T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Jan van Eyck Academie Residency 2028 (Maastrich
 t\, 11 months)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nThe Jan van Eyck Academie's
  general open call for its 2028 residency year: 30 to 32 artists\, curator
 s\, designers\, writers\, architects and other artistic researchers spend 
 11 months (15 January to 15 December 2028) in Maastricht\, across material
 -based and research-driven practices\, with access to the academy's labs a
 nd community.\n\nOrganisation: Jan van Eyck Academie\nLocation: Maastricht
 \, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settle in Maastricht an
 d register with the municipality (the academy applies for visas where rele
 vant).\nAward: Monthly stipend of EUR 1\,500 (EUR 2\,000 for participants 
 with children\; EUR 1\,500 per duo member or EUR 2\,500 combined for life 
 partners\; collectives up to EUR 4\,500 combined\, max three stipends)\, w
 ith rent including service costs deducted from the stipend. Plus a EUR 2\,
 000 annual working budget and a newly built\, furnished private studio apa
 rtment. Application fee EUR 65 excl. VAT (EUR 78.65 incl. VAT)\, waived fo
 r applicants from and living in OECD DAC-list countries\; enrolment fee fo
 r accepted participants EUR 2\,750 excl. VAT.\nDuration: 11 months\, 15 Ja
 nuary to 15 December 2028\; 30 to 32 positions\; selection outcome mid-May
  2027.\n\nMore: https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency
 -2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency-2028?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Maastricht\, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settl
 e in Maastricht and register with the municipality (the academy applies fo
 r visas where relevant).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nl-embassy-brussels-cultural-support-nov-2026@artificialnouveau.github.
 io
DTSTAMP:20261104T230337Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261103
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261104
SUMMARY:Deadline: Netherlands Embassy in Brussels: Open Call for Cultural P
 roject Support
DESCRIPTION:The Netherlands Embassy in Brussels runs several open calls per
  year subsidising Dutch-Belgian artistic and cultural projects in Belgium 
 that strengthen the Netherlands' cultural profile and promote cooperation 
 between the two countries.\n\nOrganisation: Embassy of the Kingdom of the 
 Netherlands in Brussels\nLocation: Belgium. Applicants must be professiona
 l creators\, organisations\, institutions or legal entities in Belgium wit
 h a company registration number\; the subsidy covers the Dutch side of Dut
 ch-Belgian projects.\nAward: Up to EUR 5\,000 per project.\nDuration: Roll
 ing open calls with multiple deadlines per year\; next deadlines 3 Novembe
 r 2026 and 18 March 2027.\n\nMore: https://dutchculture.nl/en/grant/nlemba
 ssy-brussels-open-call-for-support?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&u
 tm_medium=referral
URL:https://dutchculture.nl/en/grant/nlembassy-brussels-open-call-for-suppo
 rt?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Belgium. Applicants must be professional creators\, organisations\
 , institutions or legal entities in Belgium with a company registration nu
 mber\; the subsidy covers the Dutch side of Dutch-Belgian projects.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
